question_text:
The output of the following C Program is:

#include <stdio.h>
int main (void) {
    int x, *p;
    x = 30;
    p = x;
    printf("%d", *p);
    return 0;
}

explanation:
Given the fuzzy set A = {(x1, 0.3), (x2, 0.7), (x3, 0.4)}

Complement A is calculated as follows:
For x1: 1 - 0.3 = 0.7
For x2: 1 - 0.7 = 0.3
For x3: 1 - 0.4 = 0.6

Thus, the complement A = {(x1, 0.7), (x2, 0.3), (x3, 0.6)}

