question_text:
Arrange the following sets in increasing order, on the basis of their cardinality:

A. A1 = {{1,2}, {3}}
B. A2 = {{1}, {2}, {3}, {4}}
C. A3 = {{1,2,3,4,5,6}}
D. A4 = {{1,2}, {2,3,4}, {5}}
E. A5 = {{1}, {2}, {3}, {4}, {5}}

explanation:
To find the intersection A ∩ B of two fuzzy sets, we take the minimum of the membership values for each corresponding element.

Given:
A = {(x1, 0.3), (x2, 0.7), (x3, 0.4)}
B = {(x1, 0.5), (x2, 0.2), (x3, 0.5)}

We compute:
μA∩B(x1) = min(0.3, 0.5) = 0.3
μA∩B(x2) = min(0.7, 0.2) = 0.2
μA∩B(x3) = min(0.4, 0.5) = 0.4

So, A∩B = {(x1, 0.3), (x2, 0.2), (x3, 0.4)}
